// front-office-retainers.prisma — agreement templates, retainers, their versions and fee rows. Owner: Lead B (front office).
// One file per area (DB-SPLIT, studio/DEVELOPING.md): never edit another area's file
// without its owner.
//
// FO-5 (P-558, P-559, P-576, P-600; BACKLOG row FO-5 rows rev 6.2, 9, 10 part 2; contracts
// platform-and-front-office-contracts-2026-11-14.md §2.3 and §7 binding; concept fo-5s-retainer-signing r2 §3 BR-1..BR-11;
// AG-05: AG-5-3, -4, -7, -9, -34, -39, -47, -49, -50, -64, -65). This file is the schema step; the API is the row's next
// PR. Like the platform rows these carry no workspace_id (the firm is the tenant; the demo reset leaves them) and every
// table carries firm_id first in every index but its primary key. A row naming a staff member, a template, a retainer or a
// version keys on (firm_id, <id>), so it can never point at another firm's row: composite foreign keys, RESTRICT on
// delete and update, to platform_staff (firm_id, id) and to this file's own tables; the template and the retainer also
// to platform_firm (back-relation lines on platform.prisma). prospect_id, signer_person_id and company_id name FO-1a's
// fo_prospect, fo_person and fo_company: FO-1a is not on main yet, so they are plain uuids here and **FO-1k adds their
// foreign keys** (rows rev 16). Rules Prisma cannot say are in the migration (fo_retainer_ functions): status moves, one
// live retainer per prospect, versions and fee rows write-once, the template's version only grows, the hashes' and keys'
// shapes, CAD only. Money is in minor units (cents). Every value seeded or shown from here is Sample.

/// What an agreement is (rows rev 6.2): the retainer agreement, or the consultation agreement the booking sends (FO-3c).
/// An amendment or a consultation agreement never makes a client (contracts §7 §2.3-§2.4).
enum FoRetainerKind {
  RETAINER
  CONSULTATION
}

/// A retainer's state (FO-5 row; AG-05 C2). DRAFT → SENT → VIEWED → CLIENT_SIGNED → SIGNED is the signing path (FO-6
/// moves SENT onwards); DECLINED and EXPIRED come back to DRAFT by Edit and resend (AG-5-65 r1); WITHDRAWN, SIGNED and
/// SIGNED_OFFLINE are final. A request never expires once the client signed (BR-16). Moves: the migration's trigger.
enum FoRetainerStatus {
  DRAFT
  SENT
  VIEWED
  CLIENT_SIGNED
  SIGNED
  SIGNED_OFFLINE
  DECLINED
  WITHDRAWN
  EXPIRED
}

/// Who the agreement is with (BR-4): a person, or a company signed for by one of its contacts.
enum FoRetainerSubject {
  PERSON
  COMPANY
}

/// When a fee row falls due (AG-5-64 r1-r3; contracts §7 §2.3-§2.4).
enum FoRetainerFeeWhen {
  ON_SIGNING
  ON_DATE
  WHEN_SUBMITTED
  WHEN_DECIDED
  WHEN_DONE
}

/// Why a version's signing request ended (BR-9, BR-10, BR-11, BR-16): an edit made a newer version, the retainer was
/// withdrawn, signed on paper, declined or expired.
enum FoRetainerRequestEnd {
  UPDATED
  WITHDRAWN
  SIGNED_OFFLINE
  DECLINED
  EXPIRED
}

/// A firm's agreement template (BR-1; AG-5-4 r1, AG-5-7). One row per template; a new file for it makes version n+1 in
/// place (version only grows, trigger) and the earlier file stays in the file store under its own key
/// (`retainer-templates/<id>/v<n>.docx`), so a retainer keeps the template version and file it was made from. placeholders
/// are the names the file uses (read at upload; unknown names are refused by the API). Inactive templates are not offered
/// for new drafts. The name is unique in the firm.
model FoRetainerTemplate {
  id           String         @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  firmId       String         @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  name         String
  kind         FoRetainerKind @default(RETAINER)
  version      Int            @default(1)
  fileKey      String         @map("file_key")
  fileSha256   String         @map("file_sha256")
  placeholders String[]
  active       Boolean        @default(true)
  createdBy    String         @map("created_by")
  updatedBy    String         @map("updated_by")
  createdAt    DateTime       @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz
  updatedAt    DateTime       @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz

  firm      PlatformFirm @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  retainers FoRetainer[]

  @@unique([firmId, name])
  /// The target of fo_retainer's (firm_id, template_id) key.
  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@index([firmId, kind, active])
  @@map("fo_retainer_template")
}

/// A retainer (or consultation) agreement for a prospect (FO-5 row; BR-2..BR-11). The template, its version and file are
/// fixed at draft. signer_person_id is the person who signs: the prospect's person, or for a company one of its contacts
/// (empty until picked: a Corporate prospect with no SIGNATORY contact gets a warning, never a block, AG-5-50; Send needs
/// it, FO-6). The representative is an active staff member with a licence and the case-manager keys (API check, BR-3).
/// current_version is the newest fo_retainer_version's n. At most one live RETAINER per prospect: WITHDRAWN and EXPIRED
/// free the prospect for a new one (BR-10), DECLINED stays live for Edit and resend (partial unique index). Withdraw needs
/// a reason; Signed offline a PDF and a reason, and cannot be undone (status final; trigger).
model FoRetainer {
  id                    String            @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  firmId                String            @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  kind                  FoRetainerKind    @default(RETAINER)
  prospectId            String?           @map("prospect_id") @db.Uuid
  subject               FoRetainerSubject @default(PERSON)
  signerPersonId        String?           @map("signer_person_id") @db.Uuid
  companyId             String?           @map("company_id") @db.Uuid
  representativeStaffId String            @map("representative_staff_id") @db.Uuid
  templateId            String            @map("template_id") @db.Uuid
  templateVersion       Int               @map("template_version")
  templateFileKey       String            @map("template_file_key")
  status                FoRetainerStatus  @default(DRAFT)
  currentVersion        Int               @default(1) @map("current_version")
  withdrawnReason       String?           @map("withdrawn_reason")
  withdrawnAt           DateTime?         @map("withdrawn_at") @db.Timestamptz
  withdrawnBy           String?           @map("withdrawn_by")
  offlineReason         String?           @map("offline_reason")
  offlineFileKey        String?           @map("offline_file_key")
  offlineFileSha256     String?           @map("offline_file_sha256")
  offlineAt             DateTime?         @map("offline_at") @db.Timestamptz
  offlineBy             String?           @map("offline_by")
  createdBy             String            @map("created_by")
  createdAt             DateTime          @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz
  updatedAt             DateTime          @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz

  firm           PlatformFirm        @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  template       FoRetainerTemplate  @relation(fields: [firmId, templateId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  representative PlatformStaff       @relation(fields: [firmId, representativeStaffId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  versions       FoRetainerVersion[]

  /// The target of fo_retainer_version's (firm_id, retainer_id) key.
  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@index([firmId, prospectId])
  @@index([firmId, representativeStaffId])
  @@index([firmId, status])
  @@map("fo_retainer")
}

/// One version of a retainer (AG-5-3, AG-5-65; BR-7, BR-9): the merge values bound at that moment (a snapshot: a later
/// change to the person never alters it), its fee rows, the rendered file and its sha256. Write-once: only the request
/// columns change, each once (sent_at; ended_at with end_reason). An edit makes version n+1 and ends version n's request
/// (end_reason UPDATED).
model FoRetainerVersion {
  id             String                @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  firmId         String                @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  retainerId     String                @map("retainer_id") @db.Uuid
  n              Int
  mergeValues    Json                  @map("merge_values")
  fileKey        String                @map("file_key")
  originalSha256 String                @map("original_sha256")
  sentAt         DateTime?             @map("sent_at") @db.Timestamptz
  endedAt        DateTime?             @map("ended_at") @db.Timestamptz
  endReason      FoRetainerRequestEnd? @map("end_reason")
  createdBy      String                @map("created_by")
  createdAt      DateTime              @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  retainer FoRetainer         @relation(fields: [firmId, retainerId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  fees     FoRetainerFeeRow[]

  @@unique([firmId, retainerId, n])
  /// The target of fo_retainer_fee_row's (firm_id, version_id) key.
  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@map("fo_retainer_version")
}

/// A fee row of one version (BR-5; AG-5-64 r1-r3): label, amount in minor units (cents; empty while the draft has none:
/// Send needs at least one row with an amount, AG-5-9), currency CAD, when it falls due (a date only for ON_DATE).
/// Insert-only (trigger): a change is a new version.
model FoRetainerFeeRow {
  id          String            @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  firmId      String            @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  versionId   String            @map("version_id") @db.Uuid
  position    Int
  label       String
  amountMinor BigInt?           @map("amount_minor")
  currency    String            @default("CAD") @db.Char(3)
  when        FoRetainerFeeWhen
  dueOn       DateTime?         @map("due_on") @db.Date

  version FoRetainerVersion @relation(fields: [firmId, versionId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, versionId, position])
  @@map("fo_retainer_fee_row")
}
